WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.770
- We started with IBM cloud,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.940
using all public cloud instances.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.860
And as our business grew rather quickly,

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.700
we've been able to use VMware,

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.860
and basically create a Jenzabar
cloud on the IBM cloud.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.160
We use Vsphere, which
is what's used to do all

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.810
the server virtualization.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.180
We have that deployed across
multiple data centers,

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.020
which enables us to do
site to site recovery.

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.250
And that's a big advantage.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.700
So our environment is
almost a hundred percent

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.890
a hybrid environment.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:32.040
With some servers on the campus,
some servers in the cloud.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.560
We're closing in on the
four-digit server count,

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.090
and we're gonna cross that.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.890
And again, I quite counting
because the speed is so quick.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.010
We have a 99.4% retention
rate for our clients.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.850
So after they go to the
cloud, they stay there.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.990
We're continuing to move
towards cloud native,

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.640
towards the cloud as a platform.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.890
And that's based on the
positive experience we've had

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:54.810
running infrastructure

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.323
as a cloud on IBM cloud.

